### Use with REST Client (VS Code) or HTTP Client (JetBrains).
### Full documentation: docs/api.md
@base = http://localhost:8080

### Create a user. Response includes Location (new user path) and ETag: "1"
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: demo-create-1

{"email": "lan@example.com", "name": "Lan Nguyen"}

### List users (paginated). limit > 100 is capped at 100; maximum offset is 10000
GET {{base}}/api/v1/users?limit=20&offset=0

### Get one user (replace id). Save the ETag header for If-Match below
GET {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### Update with a version check: replace "1" with the ETag from GET. Wrong version => 412
### (Response includes a new ETag; repeating this request returns 412)
PATCH {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{"name": "Lan Tran"}

### Partial update without a version check: omitted fields (or null) are unchanged
PATCH {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Lan Pham"}

### --- Error examples ---

### 422: invalid input, with errors for individual fields
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "not-an-email", "name": ""}

### 409: email already exists (run after the Create user request above)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "LAN@example.com", "name": "Someone Else"}

### 415: missing Content-Type (or Content-Type other than application/json)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users

{"email": "x@example.com", "name": "X"}

### 404: malformed IDs also return 404
GET {{base}}/api/v1/users/not-a-uuid

### --- Delete (run after the error examples: 409 above requires the user to exist) ---

### DELETE does not check If-Match
DELETE {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### --- Probe ---
GET {{base}}/healthz

###
GET {{base}}/readyz
